+# PHASE K0.7A — Adjacent Read-Path Closure, MindTree Authorization & Cache Transition Verification
+
+**Date:** 2026-11-02  
+**Branch:** `arena/e77540e3-nihingobridgeupgrade`  
+**Verdict:** **PASS WITH CONDITIONS** — all confirmed adjacent Kanji exposures are closed before query/serialization; all three raw MindTree helpers now require `cms.read` plus independent source-operation clearance; one sync-status path is evidenced as non-exposing. A real rights/editorial-state cache transition cannot be exercised by the current immutable production policy architecture without mocking or changing authoritative rights state, both disallowed here. See §5.
+
+This is an addendum to, not a replacement for, [`PHASE-K0.7-KANJI-READ-PATH-ENFORCEMENT.md`](./PHASE-K0.7-KANJI-READ-PATH-ENFORCEMENT.md). K0.7 remains **BLOCKED** for publication/source clearance. This report closes its 22-path adjacent inventory and helper authorization gaps only; it does not authorize content.
+
+## 1. Scope and method
+
+The review traced all 22 exact path files carried forward from K0.7 through route handlers, direct service entry points, database query/result shapes, cache or per-call map behavior, and response serialization. No live database, migration, ingestion, production secret, browser/E2E, or production access was used. Route and service guards were tested before request parsing or database use.
+
+The existing K0.5A/B policy remains the single rights decision source. Public routes use the centralized Kanji public-delivery decision and a generic no-store 451 adapter. Direct services repeat the decision before reads/seed initialization/card hydration. No request flag, caller-provided role, provenance label, or source type can override the policy. All affected JLPT/SRS route adapters are force-dynamic and apply `Cache-Control: no-store` to success and error responses; a denial is the generic learner-safe 451 response.
+
+### 1.1 Exact 22-path classification
+
+`PROTECTED` means a centralized guard is enforced before any restricted read, seed/bootstrap, card hydration, or Kanji-bearing response, including direct service invocation. The single `NO_KANJI_EXPOSURE` result is supported by its complete serializer/query shape; it is not being marked safe merely because of its route name.
+
+| # | Exact path | Classification | Data-flow / exposure evidence and closure |
+|---:|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `src/app/api/jlpt/progress/route.ts` | **PROTECTED** | Calls `JLPTKnowledgeService.getUserProgress`; that calls `ensureInitialized`, which bootstraps the knowledge corpus and question bank before selecting sessions. The returned progress object is only user/level, counts, scores and recent session identifiers/timestamps, but the upstream bootstrap may process question-bank content. The route gate runs before the bootstrap; `JLPTKnowledgeService.getUserProgress` / `ensureInitialized` and the question-bank `TestService.ensureSeeded` bootstrap also assert the same policy before their direct work. |
+| 2 | `src/app/api/jlpt/tests/route.ts` | **PROTECTED** | `TestService.listTests` returns test names/descriptions/section configuration and question counts; question-bank provenance is not row-proven. Route plus direct service guard runs before `ensureSeeded` or query. |
+| 3 | `src/app/api/jlpt/tests/[id]/route.ts` | **PROTECTED** | `TestService.getTestById` serializes linked/fallback `Question` rows, including prompts, translations, choices, explanations and answers. Guard precedes database and seed fallback serialization. |
+| 4 | `src/app/api/jlpt/session/start/route.ts` | **PROTECTED** | `TestService.startSession` selects and returns question rows while creating session state. Guard precedes reads and insert. |
+| 5 | `src/app/api/jlpt/session/[id]/route.ts` | **PROTECTED** | `TestService.getSessionState` returns session, saved answers and hydrated question rows. Route and direct-service guards precede access. |
