+# K0.7B — Rights-Aware Cache Coherence
+
+**Verdict: PASS WITH CONDITIONS** — K0.7B’s response-cache condition is addressed with a trusted policy snapshot, a versioned cache boundary for the retained Kanji visual asset cache, removal of the unversioned database-derived MindTree result cache, no-store responses, and an app-wide client policy-version guard. Synthetic-only tests exercise the shared production resolution/cache/response-boundary contract. The production rights and editorial snapshot remains immutable and blocked; no real rights or editorial transition was performed.
+
+## 1. Scope and preserved decisions
+
+This is a bounded K0.7B addendum to K0.7 and K0.7A. It changes only application/cache boundaries, scoped tests, and this report. It does not modify rights history, source classifications, editorial decisions, memberships, ingestion, database state, migrations, or the protected K0.8 reports.
+
+K0.7A’s exact 22-path classification remains unchanged: **21 `PROTECTED`, 1 `NO_KANJI_EXPOSURE`, 0 `REQUIRES_GUARD`, 0 `UNVERIFIED`**. Its no-exposure exception remains `/api/srs/sync` GET status; the K0.7A route/direct-service tests were rerun. CMS authorization, source-operation clearance and publication approval remain separate gates. K0.7 remains blocked for public release/clearance; this phase grants no content authorization.
+
+## 2. Findings
+
+### 2.1 Effective production policy inputs
+
+Production still resolves from the immutable `K0_5A_INITIAL_RIGHTS_HISTORY`, the empty `KANJI_MEMBERSHIP_BASELINE`, and checked-in MindTree mnemonic/editorial records. Membership evidence verification and editorial release authorization remain explicitly `false`. There is no dynamic rights provider or authenticated live transition mechanism. The current production decision therefore continues to fail closed for the protected Kanji/MindTree and adjacent routes.
+
+`RIGHTS_POLICY_VERSION` was declared but previously had no cache identity effect. K0.7B now uses it as part of the trusted snapshot fingerprint. The server-side snapshot includes:
+
+- the complete immutable rights-event history, including source/scope states and event digests;
+- membership history/schema and the trusted membership-verification flag;
+- every static editorial record’s content digest, version, publication/review state, provenance and source references, plus the release-authorization flag;
+- source sets for MindTree, legacy Kanji APIs, dictionary allowlists and registered dictionary/Kanji/mixed domains;
+- pinned KanjiVG tag/archive/transformation and actual slice digest, KANJIDIC2 source/slice pin, first-party Kanji content digest, and registered-source release/domain/status/content-hash metadata.
+
+The fingerprint is an internal SHA-256 over canonicalized trusted snapshot inputs. It is not a rights decision, clearance, approval, or learner content. Malformed, unknown-version, or unhashable snapshots fail closed.
+
+### 2.2 Cache and HTTP inventory
+
+| Path/boundary | K0.7B finding and resolution |
+|---|---|
+| `KanjiLexicalGraphService.mindTreeCache` | Cached a full DB-derived MindTree graph by character, but the composed rows had no single trustworthy source version for a cache hit. Removed the persistent result cache; the aggregate is rebuilt per request after the existing direct-service policy guard. |
+| `KanjiVisualService.assetCache` | Retained only as `PolicyVersionedCache`. Its identity is policy digest + pinned KanjiVG source version + selected path and the SHA-256 of current local SVG bytes. Authorization is checked before loading and on every hit/return; policy-version mismatch fails closed. The unversioned filename index is now read per call instead of being process-cached. |
+| Next/server shared response caching | No `unstable_cache`, `use cache`, `revalidateTag`, `revalidatePath`, SWR or TanStack Query response cache was found in the inspected paths. Protected Kanji, JLPT and SRS route handlers remain dynamic and their guarded success/denial responses are `no-store`. Existing direct-service and CMS authorization checks remain intact. |
+| Dictionary APIs | `/api/dictionary`, `/api/dictionary/search`, `/api/dictionary/[id]`, and `/api/dictionary/entry/[id]` were already `force-dynamic`, and their rights-denied responses were already `no-store`; successful JSON responses lacked an explicit header. All JSON results from those four routes now use `noStoreJsonResponse`, including success, validation, not-found and error responses. Their existing rights behavior and parameter-validation order are unchanged. |
+| Client-held state / App Router | No SWR/TanStack/local-storage dictionary or Kanji payload cache was found. React state and prefetched App Router data can nevertheless remain in a long-lived tab. The root layout now passes an opaque server policy fingerprint to `PolicyVersionGuard`; it polls the no-store `/api/kanji/policy-version` endpoint every five seconds and on focus/visibility. On mismatch or an unknown status it covers the old DOM; on mismatch it reloads once for that fingerprint. Existing Kanji list/detail/vocabulary handling still clears payload state on generic 451. |
+
+The policy-version endpoint exposes only an opaque 64-character fingerprint, never source references, rights states, editorial content, or a clearance status. It is dynamic and no-store. Current public delivery remains blocked even though this metadata endpoint can return a valid fingerprint.
+
+## 3. Implementation
+
+- Added `src/lib/kanji/deliveryPolicySnapshot.ts`: trusted snapshot schema, validation, canonical digest, rights + membership + editorial decision, generic denial, and a before/after read boundary that discards output if the effective snapshot changes while asynchronous work is running.
+- Updated `src/lib/kanji/mindtreePublicDelivery.ts` to resolve only the immutable production snapshot and use that same evaluator for service guards. It introduces no production mutation/provider seam.
+- Added `src/lib/kanji/policyVersionedCache.ts` and applied it to the retained visual asset cache. Cache retrieval requires the current policy version, source version and an authorization callback; callers cannot directly get/set/clear entries.
+- Removed the unversioned MindTree aggregate cache and the process-cached KanjiVG index. The database aggregate’s source version was not trustworthy enough to key safely.
+- Updated `withKanjiPublicDeliveryGate` to use the common before/after policy boundary and preserve generic no-store 451 denial responses.
+- Added `src/lib/api/noStoreJsonResponse.ts` and applied it to all four dictionary JSON routes.
+- Added the opaque no-store policy fingerprint endpoint and `PolicyVersionGuard` to cover React/App Router state after deployment policy changes.
+- Updated the former K0.7 warm-cache sentinel test: it no longer manually inserts a stale private cache entry; it verifies the aggregate has no unversioned cache and still denies before database access.
+
+## 4. Transition and cache-coherence tests
+
+`tests/kanji-policy-cache-coherence-k07b.test.ts` uses only a private-use synthetic identity, synthetic source refs, synthetic rights events, and synthetic editorial records. It calls the same snapshot evaluator, `PolicyVersionedCache`, and response boundary used by production composition. It does not modify `K0_5A_INITIAL_RIGHTS_HISTORY`, use actual uncleared source content, manually clear cache entries, or invent a production rights provider.
+
+Coverage includes:
+
+1. Policy fingerprint changes when rights history, membership history, editorial revision, or source-version inputs change.
+2. A warm synthetic cache reuses only matching policy/source versions; a source-version change or still-allowed editorial revision gets a fresh cache identity; a stale version is rejected; and an appended synthetic rights block denies before a warm value can escape.
+3. Synthetic membership withdrawal and editorial `published` → `review` transitions deny at the shared decision contract.
+4. The shared response wrapper serves a synthetic allowed response as no-store, then returns generic no-store 451 after a rights transition without invoking the handler; it also discards an in-flight response when editorial policy changes.
+5. Unknown/malformed policy version fails closed before the handler.
+6. The policy-version endpoint exposes only an opaque no-store fingerprint; the JSON helper used by dictionary success responses sets no-store.
+
+The existing K0.7, K0.7A, dictionary rights-delivery/service, and Kanji detail rights-gate tests were rerun. No source-rights, membership or editorial records were changed.
+
+## 5. Validation
+
+- `npm run typecheck` — **PASS**.
+- Focused Vitest set: K0.7B policy/cache tests, K0.7 and K0.7A read-path tests, dictionary rights-delivery/service tests, and Kanji detail gate tests — **6 files, 26 tests passed**.
+- Scoped ESLint — **0 errors, 1 existing `@next/next/no-page-custom-font` warning** in `src/app/layout.tsx` for its existing Google Fonts `<link>`.
+- `git diff --check` — **PASS**.
+- Vite emitted the existing non-fatal CommonJS/ESM config-loader warning.
+
+No browser, E2E, database, production, deployment, or full-build validation was performed. Known DB-dependent/destructive tests were not run.
+
+## 6. Limitations and conditions
+
+- A real production rights/editorial transition remains unavailable because current policy is immutable and no authenticated live rights/membership provider exists. Tests validate the same resolver and cache/response boundary using the explicitly permitted test-only trusted snapshot contract; they do not claim a production transition occurred.
+- The five-second client poll plus focus/visibility check bounds when an already-open tab detects a new deployed snapshot; it cannot retract bytes already delivered or guarantee instantaneous revocation between checks. On mismatch the visible document is covered before reload. This is an inherent client-runtime limit and must not be described as browser-validated here.
+- The MindTree DB aggregate is intentionally uncached because a complete trustworthy row/source version is unavailable. This trades repeated query/aggregation work for fail-closed coherence. The visual asset cache remains bounded and source/policy-versioned.
+- Current membership and publication evidence remain absent/unverified; this report does not approve publication, clear sources, or lift K0.7/K0.8 blockers.
+
+## 7. Final worktree state
+
+At report completion: branch `arena/e77540e3-nihingobridgeupgrade`, HEAD `d3e4dfc2edf3852cd05a07acff711bd5e365b1fe`; **0 staged, 95 modified tracked paths, 49 untracked paths (144 status entries total)**. All changes remain uncommitted and unstaged. No reset, clean, stash, commit, push, merge, PR, deployment, database access/write, or migration was performed. Prior modified/untracked work, including all K0.8 reports, remains preserved.
